## What We Are Building
Polina's concierge drained **$100 of Anthropic credits in ~24h** after the 2026-06-24 switch to Opus 4.8. This session: diagnosed it (loop × expensive model), shipped a model-agnostic loop fix + Opus cost-hardening + a durable cost guardrail, then — when budget_log (the new tracking) showed Opus was STILL $0.4-0.7/auto-react-call even hardened — switched Polina to **gpt-5.5** (Director q6a). Separately closed two EREF dispatch bugs the run surfaced: SH13 (blocked by strict shot_id match) and SH10 (double image generation from two dispatch sources).

---

## What WORKED (with evidence) — all tsc·0 / vitest green / replay·30, pushed to origin/master
- **Diagnosis (high confidence)** — DB read-only queries: 695 concierge assistant turns in 24h post-switch, 81% auto_react. Root = watchdog↔auto-react loop (Polina re-reacted to her OWN events) × Opus uncapped-thinking + untracked cost. Corrected Agent-3's "Opus innocent" (budget_log never tracked concierge → invisible).
- **W1 loop kill** `fc2ba67` — `events.ts` suppresses `pa/notify-needed` for AI-principal's own decisions (`isSelfCausedNotify`); watchdog `pa-batch-stall-watchdog.ts` no-new-state + fresh-assistant-turn guards + `closeStaleConciergeThreads`; debounce 5s→20s. Shared `resolveOpenThreadId`.
- **W2 reasoning-off** `fc2ba67` — `conciergeReasoningParam()` sends `reasoning_effort:minimal` on anthropic branch (was dropped by isGpt5 gate → uncapped thinking).
- **W3 cost guardrail** `fc2ba67` — `lib/concierge/cost.ts`: `recordConciergeCost` → budget_log (agent_id=EXEC-CONC, episode_id set, NOT counted vs episodes.budget_spent) + daily circuit-breaker $20/24h disarms auto-react (Director chat never gated). CONFIRMED LIVE: budget_log EXEC-CONC rows appeared ($0.39-0.72/call).
- **W4.a/W5** `fc2ba67` — auto-react history 80→24, round backstop 25→6, auto-react output→800.
- **gpt-5.5 switch** (`.env.local`, gitignored) — `CONCIERGE_PROVIDER=openai`, `OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.5`. VALIDATED via micro-completion (no 400). Servers restarted, env live.
- **EREF SH13 unblock** `875b00b` — tolerant `shotIdsMatchLoose` in loadPlanOverrides (canonical plan-body vs bare event-shot).
- **EREF SH10 double-dispatch fix** `e27b5c2` — per-shot in-flight dedup at `factory.ts` Step-0 (universal chokepoint), reuses `shotIdsMatchLoose` (moved to `vgen-shot-helpers`), new `findInFlightShotDuplicate` in plan-regen-guard. Blocks only SIMULTANEOUS dup of same agent+shot; fail-open; all principals.
- **Verify**: tsc·0, vitest **1010/1010**, replay·30. Servers up (3000+8288, 30 fns).

---

## What Did NOT Work (and why)
- **Opus 4.8 for Polina, even hardened** — budget_log showed $0.39-0.72 PER auto-react call (~$84/hr extrapolated) even after reasoning-off + history-trim. Input ~39k tokens/call (fat tool-result history + full tool schemas + reasoning maybe not honored by Anthropic OpenAI-compat). My estimate of ~$0.005-0.02/call was wrong by 20-100×. → Director chose gpt-5.5 (q6a).
- **Anthropic prompt-cache via OpenAI-compat** — NOT supported (`cache_control` is native Messages API; compat shim drops it). Deferred.
- **normalizeShotId to fix bare "SH10"** — can't canonicalize a shot-only id (no scene). Used `shotIdsMatchLoose` instead.
- **Pushing the focused-sinoussi worktree** — it's 24 behind master with only stale junk (AnimaticPlayer is OLD base, −226 lines vs master; popover fix already on master a63bc45). Pushing/committing it would REGRESS master. Did NOT push it.

